#
# Rows for scripts/bench-solid.sh (format: docs/design/solid-model-json.md).
# Whitespace-separated columns; '-' = none; paths relative to the repo root
# and may use $VARIABLES (a row whose variable is unset is skipped).
#
# name             kind       reference                                      model                                           project  stages
two_rooms_synth    synthetic  tests/fixtures/solid_model/two_rooms.plan.json tests/fixtures/solid_model/two_rooms.detected.json -        -
# The office_corridor fixture (sensor frames only) has no authored reference
# yet (W0.6 authors NewOffice's); until then this row runs the stage DAG on a
# copy and scores the project's model against the synthetic plan only to
# prove the project path runs end to end: every metric is n/a until the
# solid-model stages exist (append them to 'stages' as they land). 'mesh' is
# left out: its two vertical planes give the MIP 0 cells, so the fit metrics
# stay n/a on this fixture.
office_corridor    fixture    tests/fixtures/solid_model/two_rooms.plan.json -                                               tests/fixtures/scans/office_corridor.rux clouds,planes,rooms
# Local-only rows (never committed data), skipped unless the variable is set:
# NewOffice: the authored reference is committed (DRAFT, reusex-z1v.2.6); the
# scan is not. Point $REUSEX_NEWOFFICE_RUX at a copy of NewOffice's
# project.rux regenerated with today's defaults on the poses the reference
# was authored on (reusex-s4t):
#   cp ~/repos/NewOffice/project.rux newoffice-regen.rux
#   sqlite3 newoffice-regen.rux \
#     'UPDATE sensor_frames SET transform = initial_transform;'
#   rux -p newoffice-regen.rux create clouds   # defaults (sampling factor 4)
#   rux -p newoffice-regen.rux create planes   # defaults (adaptive)
# The reference was drawn on the April cloud, built from the frames'
# initial_transform; their stored transform has since moved (median 4 cm,
# up to 16 cm, non-rigid), so a cloud rebuilt from it disagrees with the
# reference by up to ~0.3 m in the WC row. A fresh `import rtabmap` of
# database.db gives the same trajectory but rotated 2.08 deg about the
# vertical, so it cannot be scored against this reference at all.
# (2026-10-17, main 840cf8dc, chain storeys..spaces: room IoU 0.874 / +2,
# wall rms 0.054 m, openings 0.62 / 0.70 -- vs the legacy unregenerated
# copy 0.893 / +1, 0.141 m, 0.24 / 0.30.)
newoffice         local      tests/fixtures/solid_model/newoffice.plan.yaml -                                               $REUSEX_NEWOFFICE_RUX storeys,classify,walls,openings
# s3dis_area1      local      $REUSEX_S3DIS_DIR/area1.plan.json             -                                               $REUSEX_S3DIS_DIR/area1.rux storeys,walls,spaces,openings
# house1 / house2 (scan archive, see reusex-yf4.3): authored references
# committed (DRAFT, maintainer review pending), scans not. Point the variables
# at a copy of each project.rux whose clouds/planes were regenerated (sensor-
# oriented normals): the references use the detected level frames, which the
# row's storeys stage re-detects (deterministic). house1 = one storey with a
# split level; house2 = two storeys in their own frames, heavily drifted.
# The local rows run storeys -> classify -> walls (WP3, reusex-z1v.5.7) ->
# openings (WP5, reusex-z1v.7.5), so they score the wall metrics
# (wall_recall / wall_precision / wall_position_rms_m /
# wall_thickness_err_mean_m / _p95_m) and the opening line: opening_recall /
# opening_precision / opening_iou_mean (a match: rectangle IoU >= 0.5 in the
# reference wall's face, `rux analyze solid --opening-iou`), gated by
# bench-solid-compare.py.
house1            local      tests/fixtures/solid_model/house1.plan.yaml    -                                               $REUSEX_HOUSE1_RUX storeys,classify,walls,openings
house2            local      tests/fixtures/solid_model/house2.plan.yaml    -                                               $REUSEX_HOUSE2_RUX storeys,classify,walls,openings
